<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<Version>10.2.0</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>10.2.0: built SQL is laid out for people to read by default (SqlBuilderOptions.Layout = SqlLayout.Readable): each clause starts a line, a list with more than one item puts each item on its own indented line, AND / OR in conditions start indented lines, and CREATE TABLE / INSERT column lists, a single VALUES row and subqueries open indented blocks. Only the whitespace between tokens changes (literals, quoted identifiers, comments and dollar-quoted bodies are copied as they are) and the layout allocates nothing beyond the result. Use SqlBuilderOptions.Compact (Layout = SqlLayout.Compact) for the previous one-line form; code that compares built SQL text with one-line strings needs Compact or new expectations. New: SqlFormatter.Format(sql, dialect) applies the layout to any SQL; SqlBuilderOptions.Readable and SqlBuilderOptions.Compact presets. In / NotIn take any ISpanFormattable (In&lt;T&gt;): numbers, Guids and dates are written inline in the dialect's literal syntax, and a type with no SQL literal (TimeSpan, enums, record ids, NaN) is bound; In / NotIn(string) and (char) bind every value as a parameter, and In('a') no longer writes the character's code (97) through the long overload. SqlBuilderOptions.StrictTypes is now on by default: typed comparisons (Where&lt;T&gt;, On&lt;T&gt;, Set&lt;T&gt;, ...) throw SqlBuildException (TypeMismatch) for a value of the wrong type, including every value of an IN list, and for IS NULL on a non-nullable column; set StrictTypes = false for the previous behavior. New: ISqlParameterValue&lt;TValue&gt; marks a wrapper that binds as TValue, so a column of that type compares as TValue (RecordID&lt;T&gt; is ISqlParameterValue&lt;Guid&gt;, AutoRecordID&lt;T&gt; is ISqlParameterValue&lt;long&gt;). Stages are single-use and share one pooled per-thread writer: continuing a stage that a later stage moved past, or one whose statement was already built or streamed, throws InvalidOperationException. Build() / BuildSql() can be called again on the same stage and return the same SqlResult; WriteTo on an unbuilt stage is final. Fixed: WHERE kept its clause flag when the comparison copied the writer.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<RootNamespace>Jakar.SqlBuilder</RootNamespace>
		<AssemblyName>Jakar.SqlBuilder</AssemblyName>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Description>Easy Sql Building</Description>
		<PackageId>Jakar.SqlBuilder</PackageId>
		<Authors>Tyler Stegmaier</Authors>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Jakar510/Jakar.Database</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Jakar510/Jakar.Database</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\icon.png" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="True" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
		<DefineConstants>DEBUG;TRACE</DefineConstants>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Dapper.Contrib" />
		<PackageReference Include="Jakar.Extensions" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
